Fillets: where the mid-point of a rolling ball's contacts lies on the
guide's polar axis, the walk's section condition is taken on the ball's
centre, so that it still picks a ball (mitcad#1368).

The walked constant-radius blend (BlendFunc_ConstRad, and
BlendFunc_ConstRadInv for its ends on restrictions) picks the ball for the
guide's parameter by the mid-point of its contact points lying in the
guide's normal plane (patch 0075). Where that mid-point lies on the guide's
polar axis (the line through its centre of curvature square to its
osculating plane), the condition holds the ball no more: a pocket's floor
square to a concave wall arc of radius R, rounded with exactly 2 R, puts
the ball's floor contact R from the arc's axis on its far side and its
wall contact R from it on the near side, so the mid-point of every ball
round the arc lies on the axis, which every normal plane of the arc holds.
The solver returned the start section at every step (its Jacobian
singular, the tangents not found) and the walk halved its step to nothing;
at 0.79999 and 0.80001 for R = 0.4 it built. The inverse function lost its
hold on the guide's parameter the same way.

Both functions now test |1 - k (M - P).n| (M the mid-point, P the guide's
point, k its curvature, n its principal normal: the derivative of the
condition by the guide's arc length) and below 1e-6 take the condition on
the ball's centre (the mean of the centres seen from both contacts), with
its first and second derivatives. Where the ball's section lies in the
guide's normal plane, as between surfaces of revolution about the axis of
a circular guide, both conditions pick the same ball; elsewhere the
mid-point stays the condition, unchanged.

Test: geometry/tests/test_fillet_ball_twice_arc.cpp, a pocket whose floor
meets concave arcs of 0.4, rounded with 0.8 (and 0.79999, 0.80001) by
OCCT's fillet alone and by MitCad's, and the reported body (a case of
MITCAD_GEOMETRY_CASES): the rounding builds at exactly 0.8, valid, without
MitCad's 0.1 % smaller retry, and on the pocket it lies within 1e-4 mm of
the roundings at 0.79999 and 0.80001 (6e-6 mm measured). Without the
patch OCCT's fillet is not done at 0.8 (one faulty contour).

Upstream: new.

